  "implementation": [
    "Strict closed semantic type/body/binding/public frontiers now admit nominal data and phantom arguments. Physical input schemas and rebuilt result schema are part of a distinct key; runtime words/literals remain parameters.",
    "Recursively reject owners, borrowed roots, host values, demands and callables from this plain-value ABI. Unsupported scoped/existential/generative/private evidence still declines sharing.",
    "Direct generic projection from a nominal stored record now uses the same checked dataField evidence as planValue/emission and maps its field type. It no longer requires a nonexistent associated getter.",
    "Completed nominal admission uses the same full contextual keys and conservative call-depth accounting. The first executable root walk still reconstructs inference; keys are recomputed after admission.",
    "Post-admission key construction reuses the already-built result schema. Strict keys also allow anonymous wrappers previously excluded by the narrower row-frontier gate; each of read/twice/outer now shares once."
  ],
  "workload": "Generic read of three U32 fields from a nominal Row; six stages call their predecessor twice; one/four/eight repeated top-level calls. Every build executes inputs1/7/41 against independent field-sum/stage-count recurrence.",
